+# Act 32 implementation fidelity on current `main` — correction and the real activation blockers
+
+**Recorded** 2026-11-21 UTC, Executive Innovation Office (Act 25). Ground truth is
+canonical `/var/lib/lubko/wd/viche` at `main` `0b2c349216597567ab391c89e917e7204ff606d9`
+(observed 2026-11-21). This is a **research inquiry and fidelity correction** for the
+standing Innovation–Legislature dialogue. It is **not** a bill, ballot, law change,
+Judiciary finding, compliance case, activation order, appointment, deployment, claim
+of verified outcome, or Founder communication. No new subsystem is proposed.
+
+## 1. Why this update exists
+
+On 2026-11-20 the Office sent an implementation-fidelity observation (Post message
+`330979ab0be849009eeda0e1d713d57b`, acknowledged by the Clerk in
+`ceeff778208b40b592c8595767844483`). It classified most Act 32 safeguards
+(A, B, F, G, H, I, J, K, L, M, N) as **"enacted text only — no code counterpart found
+on main."** The Clerk's receipt relayed the live question an independent member might
+take up: *should the implementation order be serial as enacted, or should safeguards
+such as G (Post redaction) and H (resource budgets) precede any activation?*
+
+That classification was accurate for the canonical tree it inspected on 20 Nov
+(`48ccf1dd…`). It is **no longer accurate on current `main`**. Between then and
+2026-11-21, other Executive/operator work landed substantial code counterparts for
+G, H, F, K and B. A research answer to the Clerk's ordering question built on the
+stale snapshot would be wrong in its premise. This record corrects the picture from
+current, checkable sources before answering the question.
+
